.TH EUCLID-CLI-ENS-DELETE-TOPIC-TAG 1 "August 2026" "euclid-cli 1.0.53" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-ens-delete-topic-tag \- delete a tag from a topic
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli ens delete-topic-tag
.BR \-\-topic | \-t
.I ERN
.BR \-\-key | \-k
.I KEY
.SH DESCRIPTION
Deletes a tag from a topic identified by its Euclid resource name (ERN).
Deleting a key the topic does not have is not an error.
.PP
The
.I euclid:application
tag records which application owns the topic and is written by
.BR euclid-cli-eap-apply (1);
only an administrator may change it, and anyone else is refused with
.IR "HTTP 403" .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-topic " " \fIERN\fR
Euclid resource name of the topic to remove the tag from. Required.
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-key " " \fIKEY\fR
Key of the tag to delete. Required.
.PP
The topic may be given by
.B name
instead of by ERN, in which case it is resolved in your session's account
and namespace; see
.B NAMES AND ERNS
in
.BR euclid-cli-ens (1).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The tag was deleted. No output is printed.
.TP
.B 1
Missing/invalid arguments, the server could not be reached, no topic
with that name or ERN exists, or the tag is one only an administrator
may change.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 ens delete-topic-tag \e
    --topic ern:ens:eu-central-1:000000000000:development:topic:order-events \e
    --key team
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-ens (1),
.BR euclid-cli-ens-add-topic-tag (1),
.BR euclid-cli-ens-set-topic-tag (1)
